{"format":"vetro-plugin","version":1,"manifest":{"id":"art-sql","name":"Art SQL API","version":"0.1.0","apiVersion":1,"permissions":["exec"],"author":"bertrandom","description":"Read-only SQL over HTTP (Datasette-style JSON) for the Art app's artapp.db, on its own LAN port with an API key. Uses the TV's sqlite3. No outbound connections.","main":"index.js","ui":{"label":"Art SQL"}},"files":{"README.md":"# Art SQL API\n\nA read-only HTTP API over the Samsung **Art app's** database (`artapp.db`), so another app on your network can send SQL and\nget JSON back. The URLs and JSON follow a subset of [Datasette](https://datasette.io)'s JSON API, so a client written\nfor Datasette mostly works. This is **not** Datasette and is not affiliated with it: it is a few hundred lines of Node and the\nTV's own `sqlite3`.\n\n## Use\n\n1. Install it, switch it on, open the **Art SQL** tab. It shows the endpoint (`http://TV-IP:8642/artapp.json`) and an\n   API key.\n2. Send the key as `Authorization: Bearer <key>` (or `X-API-Key: <key>`, or `?_key=<key>` for a quick test in a\n   browser, though that puts the key in URLs and logs).\n\n```sh\nKEY=...   # from the tab\ncurl -H \"Authorization: Bearer $KEY\" 'http://192.168.1.45:8642/artapp.json'                      # tables and columns\ncurl -H \"Authorization: Bearer $KEY\" 'http://192.168.1.45:8642/artapp.json?sql=select+count(*)+as+n+from+sqlite_master'\ncurl -H \"Authorization: Bearer $KEY\" 'http://192.168.1.45:8642/artapp/Content.json?_size=20&ArtistName__contains=Monet'\ncurl -H \"Authorization: Bearer $KEY\" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n     -d '{\"sql\":\"select ContentID, ArtworkTitle from Content where ArtistName = :artist\",\"params\":{\"artist\":\"Claude Monet\"}}' 'http://192.168.1.45:8642/artapp.json'\n```\n\nThe tab also has a box to try queries and a list of tables you can click.\n\n## API\n\n| Request | Answer |\n| --- | --- |\n| `GET /.json` | the one database: `{\"artapp\": {...}}` |\n| `GET /-/versions.json` | sqlite3 version and this Shard's version |\n| `GET /artapp.json` | `{\"ok\": true, \"tables\": [{\"name\", \"type\", \"columns\": [...]}]}` |\n| `GET /artapp.json?sql=…` | run a query. `:name` in the SQL is filled from `?name=value` (always as a string, as Datasette does) |\n| `POST /artapp.json` | the same, with a JSON body `{\"sql\": \"…\", \"params\": {\"name\": \"value\"}}`, for long queries |\n| `GET /artapp/<table>.json` | rows of one table: `?_size=` (default 100), `?_sort=` / `?_sort_desc=`, `?_next=` (from the previous page's `next`), and filters `?col=value`, `?col__gt=`, `__gte`, `__lt`, `__lte`, `__not`, `__contains`, `__startswith`, `__endswith`, `__like`, `__glob`, `__isnull=1`, `__notnull=1` |\n\nThe answer to a query is\n\n```json\n{\"ok\": true, \"database\": \"artapp\", \"query\": {\"sql\": \"…\", \"params\": {}}, \"columns\": [\"…\"], \"rows\": [{\"…\": \"…\"}],\n \"truncated\": false, \"query_ms\": 41}\n```\n\n`?_shape=array` gives just the rows (`[{…}, {…}]`), `?_shape=array&_nl=on` gives one JSON object per line,\n`?_shape=arrays` gives `{\"columns\": [...], \"rows\": [[...], ...]}`, and `?_shape=objects` gives `{\"rows\": [...]}`.\nErrors are `{\"ok\": false, \"error\": \"…\", \"status\": 400, \"title\": \"Invalid SQL\"}` with that HTTP status; a wrong key is\n`401`, a full queue is `429`.\n\nA query returns at most **1000 rows** (the *Row limit* setting); past that `truncated` is `true`. CORS is open (`*`) by\ndefault so a web page can call the API with the key; set an origin, or nothing, on the tab.\n\n**Differences from Datasette:** one database, read-only, JSON only (no HTML pages), `_next` is a row offset instead of a\nkeyset token, `columns` is empty for a query with no rows, there is no `_where`, `_facet`, `_col`, row pages or\n`/-/metadata`, integers above 2^53 lose precision (they pass through JSON), and a blob comes back as whatever text\nsqlite3 prints for it (use `hex(col)` in the query for something reliable).\n\n## What it can and cannot run\n\nThe query runs in the TV's `sqlite3` shell **as root**, with `-readonly`. Read-only stops writes to the database, but the\nshell has functions that reach the file system, and the TV's sqlite3 (3.33.0 on the tested TV) is older than the\n`-safe` flag (3.37) that turns them off. So the Shard checks every query first ([`sql.js`](sql.js)):\n\n- **One statement**, starting with `SELECT`, `WITH`, `VALUES`, `PRAGMA` (reading only: no `=`) or `EXPLAIN`.\n  `SELECT`/`WITH`/`VALUES` run as `SELECT * FROM (<your query>) LIMIT <row limit + 1>`.\n- **These words are refused anywhere in the text**, even quoted or inside a string: `attach`, `detach`, `vacuum`,\n  `readfile`, `writefile`, `edit`, `fsdir`, `zipfile`, `load_extension`, `sha3_query`, `fts3_tokenizer`,\n  `temp_store_directory`, `data_store_directory`. So a column named `edit` cannot be queried by name (use `select *`), and\n  `where note like '%edit%'` is refused too: pass the text as a parameter (`where note like :q`, `?q=%25edit%25`), which\n  is not scanned.\n- The SQL reaches the shell base64-encoded, so no character of it is seen by `sh`. A string or blob is capped at 10 MB\n  (`.limit length`), and a query is stopped after the *Time limit* (10 s by default, up to 30 s).\n\nTreat the API key like a password: anyone with it can read everything in the Art app's database.\n\n## Permissions\n\n`exec`: the database is in the Art app's sandbox (`/opt/usr/home/owner/apps_rw/org.tizen.art-app/`, Smack label\n`User::Pkg::org.tizen.art-app`), which Vetro's own user cannot read, so the query runs as root through Vetro's agent.\n\n## Commands it runs\n\nAll through `ctx.execute`, as root.\n\n| When | Command | Why |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| the Shard starts, the database path changes, **Check sqlite3** | `/usr/bin/sqlite3 -version`; `[ -r <database> ]` | find out whether sqlite3 is there and new enough (3.33+, for JSON output), and whether the file exists |\n| every query, from the API or the tab | `__q=\"$(printf %s <base64 SQL> \\| base64 -d)\"; exec /usr/bin/sqlite3 -readonly -batch -bail -cmd '.timeout 3000' -cmd '.limit length 10000000' -cmd '.mode json' <database> \"$__q\" </dev/null` | run the checked query read-only and get JSON. `.timeout` waits up to 3 s if the Art app is writing |\n\nQueries run one at a time, because every Vetro command shares one queue; up to 8 more wait, after that the API answers `429`.\nA long query makes the rest of Vetro wait too, which is why the time limit is capped at 30 s.\n\n## Network\n\nIt opens no outbound connection. It listens on **one port** (default **8642**, set on the tab; 8001 and 8002 are taken by Samsung's own `msf-server` on every Samsung TV), bound to all interfaces\n(`0.0.0.0`), plain HTTP. Every request except a CORS preflight needs the API key. The key travels in clear over HTTP,\nso keep the TV on a trusted network and **never forward this port to the Internet**.\n\n## Data it keeps\n\nIts own `config.json`: the API key, the port, the database path, the CORS origin, the time and row limits. It keeps no\nquery results and no log of queries; the tab shows only counters and the last error. Removing the Shard deletes the key.\n\n## Effect on the Art app\n\nThe file is opened read-only with a rollback journal (the tested database has `artapp.db-journal`, not WAL), so a query\ncreates no files next to the database and changes nothing in it. While a query reads, the Art app cannot write for that\nmoment; if the Art app is writing, the query waits up to 3 s and then fails with `database is locked`. This is not\nsupported by Samsung, and a firmware update may move or change the database.\n\n## Tested\n\n_Off-device_ (macOS, Node 26), with the same end-to-end suite run against **sqlite3 3.33.0** (built from the official\namalgamation, the version the tested TV has) and 3.53: every endpoint and `_shape`, table filters and paging,\nparameters (including an injection attempt through one), the API key, CORS preflight, 27 queries that must be refused,\nthe queue limit, the time limit, and switching off with requests in flight. On 3.33.0 it also confirmed that\n`readfile()`, `writefile()` and `fsdir()` work despite `-readonly` and that `-safe` does not exist, which is why the\nchecks above are needed, and that a query leaves the database and its journal byte-for-byte unchanged and creates no\nfiles. 3.33.0 echoes the `.limit` line to stdout; the Shard strips it.\n\n_On the TV_ — Samsung The Frame **QN75LS03B** (2022), Tizen 6.5, `/usr/bin/sqlite3` 3.33.0, Vetro 0.5.0, installed in\nDeveloper mode, queried with `curl` over the LAN on port 8642:\n\n- no key and a wrong key get `401`; `/-/versions.json`, `/artapp.json` (16 tables and views, 285 columns) and queries\n  answer `200`; a `group by` over the 9,358 rows of `Content` takes about 0.7 s, small queries 10-130 ms;\n- `:name` parameters (GET and POST), `/artapp/Content.json` paging with `next_url`, `_shape=array|objects`, and the\n  1000-row cap (`truncated: true`) work;\n- `readfile()` and `DELETE` are refused with `400`, a bad column gives sqlite3's own message, the CORS preflight is `204`;\n- the Art app's database folder is unchanged afterwards: the same two files, owner, Smack label and timestamps.\n\nPort 8001, the first default, is taken by Samsung's `msf-server` on every Samsung TV, hence 8642.\n","index.js":"'use strict';\n// Art SQL API: a read-only HTTP API over the Samsung Art app's database (artapp.db), so another app on the network\n// can send SQL and get JSON back. The URLs and JSON follow a subset of Datasette's JSON API (it is not Datasette).\n//\n// How a query runs: this Shard listens on its own port (Vetro's /plugins/<id>/api routes need a paired device or the\n// page's session token, which another app does not have), checks the API key, checks the SQL (sql.js), then runs the\n// TV's own /usr/bin/sqlite3 with -readonly as root through ctx.execute, because the file sits in the Art app's\n// sandbox. One query at a time: every Vetro command shares one queue. Plain ES5: older TVs run Node 4.4.\n\nvar http = require('http'), crypto = require('crypto'), fs = require('fs'), path = require('path'), os = require('os');\nvar querystring = require('querystring');\nvar Q = require('./sql.js');\n\nvar DEFAULTS = { port: 8642, dbPath: '/opt/usr/home/owner/apps_rw/org.tizen.art-app/data/db/artapp.db', sqlite: '/usr/bin/sqlite3',\n    cors: '*', timeoutMs: 10000, maxRows: 1000 };\nvar MAX_TIMEOUT = 30000, MAX_ROWS = 5000, MAX_PENDING = 8, MAX_BODY = 65536, MAX_SOCKETS = 32, VERSION = '0.1.0';\n\nfunction validPath(p) { return typeof p === 'string' && p.charAt(0) === '/' && p.length <= 1024 && /^[A-Za-z0-9._\\/-]+$/.test(p) && !/(^|\\/)\\.\\.(\\/|$)/.test(p); }\nfunction validOrigin(o) { return o === '*' || o === '' || (typeof o === 'string' && o.length <= 200 && /^https?:\\/\\/[A-Za-z0-9.:\\[\\]-]+$/.test(o)); }\nfunction dbName(p) { return path.basename(p).replace(/\\.[^.]*$/, '').replace(/[^A-Za-z0-9_-]/g, '_') || 'db'; }\n// Constant-time compare without crypto.timingSafeEqual (Node 6.6+).\nfunction sameKey(a, b) { a = String(a || ''); b = String(b || ''); if (!a || a.length !== b.length) return false; var d = 0; for (var i = 0; i < a.length; i++) d |= a.charCodeAt(i) ^ b.charCodeAt(i); return d === 0; }\nfunction newKey() { return crypto.randomBytes(24).toString('hex'); }\n\nfunction readBody(req, cb) {\n    var chunks = [], size = 0, done = false;\n    req.on('data', function (c) { size += c.length; if (size > MAX_BODY) { if (!done) { done = true; cb(new Error('Request too large')); } if (req.destroy) req.destroy(); return; } chunks.push(c); });\n    req.on('end', function () { if (!done) { done = true; cb(null, Buffer.concat(chunks).toString('utf8')); } });\n    req.on('error', function (e) { if (!done) { done = true; cb(e); } });\n}\nfunction parseJsonObject(text) { var p = JSON.parse(text || '{}'); if (!p || typeof p !== 'object' || Array.isArray(p)) throw new Error('Body must be a JSON object'); return p; }\n\nfunction lanAddresses() {\n    var out = [];\n    try { var ifs = os.networkInterfaces(); Object.keys(ifs).forEach(function (k) { (ifs[k] || []).forEach(function (a) { if (a.family === 'IPv4' || a.family === 4) { if (!a.internal) out.push(a.address); } }); }); } catch (e) { /* none */ }\n    return out;\n}\n\nfunction loadPage(ctx) {\n    var places = [path.join(__dirname, 'ui.html'), path.join(ctx.dir || '', 'ui.html')];\n    for (var i = 0; i < places.length; i++) { try { return fs.readFileSync(places[i], 'utf8'); } catch (e) { /* next */ } }\n    return '<!doctype html><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><p>Page file missing: reinstall this Shard.</p>';\n}\n\nmodule.exports = function (ctx) {\n    var server = null, sockets = [], page = null, running = false, queue = [], busy = false, stopped = true;\n    var sqliteVersion = null, probeError = null, lastError = null, listenError = null, counts = { queries: 0, errors: 0, denied: 0 };\n\n    function cfg() {\n        var c; try { c = ctx.config.get(); } catch (e) { c = {}; }\n        if (!c || typeof c !== 'object' || Array.isArray(c)) c = {};\n        var out = {};\n        Object.keys(DEFAULTS).forEach(function (k) { out[k] = DEFAULTS[k]; });\n        if (typeof c.port === 'number' && c.port >= 1024 && c.port <= 65535 && c.port % 1 === 0) out.port = c.port;\n        if (validPath(c.dbPath)) out.dbPath = c.dbPath;\n        if (validPath(c.sqlite)) out.sqlite = c.sqlite;   // not on the page: only for a TV that keeps sqlite3 elsewhere\n        if (validOrigin(c.cors)) out.cors = c.cors;\n        if (typeof c.timeoutMs === 'number' && c.timeoutMs >= 1000 && c.timeoutMs <= MAX_TIMEOUT) out.timeoutMs = Math.round(c.timeoutMs);\n        if (typeof c.maxRows === 'number' && c.maxRows >= 1 && c.maxRows <= MAX_ROWS) out.maxRows = Math.round(c.maxRows);\n        out.apiKey = typeof c.apiKey === 'string' && /^[0-9a-f]{32,}$/.test(c.apiKey) ? c.apiKey : null;\n        return out;\n    }\n    function save(patch) {\n        var c; try { c = ctx.config.get(); } catch (e) { c = {}; }\n        if (!c || typeof c !== 'object' || Array.isArray(c)) c = {};\n        Object.keys(patch).forEach(function (k) { c[k] = patch[k]; });\n        ctx.config.set(c);\n    }\n    function apiKey() { var k = cfg().apiKey; if (!k) { k = newKey(); try { save({ apiKey: k }); } catch (e) { /* keep it for this run */ } } return k; }\n\n    // ---- running queries, one at a time ----\n    function exec(sqlText, timeoutMs) {\n        var c = cfg();\n        return Promise.resolve().then(function () { return ctx.execute(Q.command(c.sqlite, c.dbPath, sqlText), timeoutMs || c.timeoutMs); });\n    }\n    function enqueue(job) {\n        return new Promise(function (resolve, reject) {\n            if (queue.length >= MAX_PENDING) { var e = new Error('Too many queries waiting; try again shortly'); e.status = 429; e.title = 'Busy'; return reject(e); }\n            queue.push({ job: job, resolve: resolve, reject: reject }); pump();\n        });\n    }\n    function pump() {\n        if (busy || !queue.length) return;\n        var item = queue.shift(); busy = true;\n        var p; try { p = item.job(); } catch (e) { p = Promise.reject(e); }\n        p.then(function (v) { busy = false; item.resolve(v); pump(); }, function (e) { busy = false; item.reject(e); pump(); });\n    }\n    // Check, run and parse one query. Resolves { rows, columns, truncated, sql, params, ms }.\n    function query(sqlText, params, maxRows) {\n        var c = cfg(), limit = maxRows || c.maxRows, prep;\n        try { prep = Q.prepare(sqlText, params, limit); } catch (e) { return Promise.reject(e); }\n        return enqueue(function () {\n            var t0 = Date.now();\n            return exec(prep.sql).then(function (r) {\n                r = r || {};\n                if (r.timed_out) { var te = new Error('Query took longer than ' + (c.timeoutMs / 1000) + ' s'); te.status = 400; te.title = 'Query timed out'; throw te; }\n                if (r.exit_code !== 0) { var se = new Error(Q.cleanError(r.stderr || r.stdout)); se.status = 400; se.title = 'Invalid SQL'; throw se; }\n                var rows;\n                try { rows = Q.parseOutput(r.stdout, prep.first); } catch (e) { var pe = new Error('Could not read sqlite3 output: ' + e.message); pe.status = 500; throw pe; }\n                var truncated = prep.wrapped && rows.length > limit; if (truncated) rows = rows.slice(0, limit);\n                counts.queries++;\n                return { rows: rows, columns: Q.columnsOf(rows), truncated: truncated, sql: sqlText, params: prep.params, ms: Date.now() - t0 };\n            });\n        });\n    }\n\n    // Is sqlite3 there, which version, and can root read the file? Runs at start and from the page.\n    function probe() {\n        var c = cfg();\n        var cmd = Q.shQuote(c.sqlite) + ' -version 2>&1; [ -r ' + Q.shQuote(c.dbPath) + ' ] && echo __READABLE__ || echo __MISSING__';\n        return Promise.resolve().then(function () { return ctx.execute(cmd, 5000); }).then(function (r) {\n            var out = String((r && r.stdout) || ''), m = /^(\\d+)\\.(\\d+)\\.(\\d+)/m.exec(out);\n            sqliteVersion = m ? m[0] : null;\n            if (!m) probeError = 'sqlite3 not found at ' + c.sqlite;\n            else if (+m[1] < 3 || (+m[1] === 3 && +m[2] < 33)) probeError = 'sqlite3 ' + m[0] + ' is too old (JSON output needs 3.33.0)';\n            else if (out.indexOf('__READABLE__') < 0) probeError = 'Database not found: ' + c.dbPath;\n            else probeError = null;\n        }, function (e) { probeError = 'Could not run sqlite3: ' + (e && e.message || e); }).then(function () { return state(); });\n    }\n\n    // ---- HTTP ----\n    function cors(res) {\n        var o = cfg().cors;\n        if (!o) return;\n        res.setHeader('Access-Control-Allow-Origin', o);\n        res.setHeader('Access-Control-Allow-Headers', 'Authorization, Content-Type');\n        res.setHeader('Access-Control-Allow-Methods', 'GET, POST, OPTIONS');\n        res.setHeader('Access-Control-Max-Age', '600');\n        if (o !== '*') res.setHeader('Vary', 'Origin');\n    }\n    function send(res, code, body, nl) {\n        var text = nl ? body.map(function (r) { return JSON.stringify(r); }).join('\\n') + (body.length ? '\\n' : '') : JSON.stringify(body);\n        res.writeHead(code, { 'content-type': nl ? 'application/x-ndjson; charset=utf-8' : 'application/json; charset=utf-8', 'cache-control': 'no-store' });\n        res.end(text);\n    }\n    function sendError(res, e) {\n        var status = e && e.status || 500;\n        if (status >= 500) counts.errors++;\n        lastError = String(e && e.message || e);\n        send(res, status, { ok: false, error: lastError, status: status, title: e && e.title || (status === 401 ? 'Unauthorized' : 'Error') });\n    }\n    // Datasette's _shape: default (objects plus metadata), array, arrays, objects; _nl=on with array for NDJSON.\n    function shaped(res, q, d, extra) {\n        var shape = q._shape || '';\n        if (shape === 'array') return send(res, 200, d.rows, q._nl === 'on');\n        if (shape === 'arrays') return send(res, 200, { ok: true, columns: d.columns, rows: d.rows.map(function (r) { return d.columns.map(function (k) { return r[k]; }); }), truncated: d.truncated });\n        if (shape === 'objects') return send(res, 200, { ok: true, rows: d.rows, truncated: d.truncated });\n        var body = { ok: true, database: dbName(cfg().dbPath), query: { sql: d.sql, params: d.params }, columns: d.columns, rows: d.rows, truncated: d.truncated, query_ms: d.ms };\n        if (extra) Object.keys(extra).forEach(function (k) { body[k] = extra[k]; });\n        send(res, 200, body);\n    }\n    function authorized(req, q) {\n        var h = String(req.headers.authorization || ''), m = /^Bearer\\s+(\\S+)$/i.exec(h), given = m ? m[1] : (q._key || req.headers['x-api-key']);\n        return sameKey(given, apiKey());\n    }\n    function paramsFrom(q) { var p = {}; Object.keys(q).forEach(function (k) { if (k !== 'sql' && k.charAt(0) !== '_') p[k] = [].concat(q[k])[0]; }); return p; }\n\n    function handle(req, res) {\n        try {\n            cors(res);\n            if (req.method === 'OPTIONS') { res.writeHead(204); res.end(); return; }\n            var raw = String(req.url || '/'), qi = raw.indexOf('?'), q = querystring.parse(qi < 0 ? '' : raw.slice(qi + 1)), p;\n            try { p = decodeURIComponent(qi < 0 ? raw : raw.slice(0, qi)); } catch (e) { return send(res, 400, { ok: false, error: 'Bad URL', status: 400 }); }\n            if (!authorized(req, q)) {\n                counts.denied++;\n                res.setHeader('WWW-Authenticate', 'Bearer');\n                return send(res, 401, { ok: false, error: 'Missing or wrong API key: send \"Authorization: Bearer <key>\"', status: 401, title: 'Unauthorized' });\n            }\n            var name = dbName(cfg().dbPath), m;\n            if (req.method !== 'GET' && req.method !== 'POST') return send(res, 405, { ok: false, error: 'GET or POST only', status: 405 });\n            if (p === '/' || p === '/.json') {\n                var dbs = {}; dbs[name] = { name: name, path: '/' + name, is_mutable: false };\n                return send(res, 200, dbs);\n            }\n            if (p === '/-/versions.json' || p === '/-/versions') return send(res, 200, { sqlite: { version: sqliteVersion }, shard: { name: 'art-sql', version: VERSION }, datasette_compatible: 'JSON API subset' });\n            if (p === '/' + name || p === '/' + name + '.json') {\n                if (req.method === 'POST') {\n                    return readBody(req, function (err, text) {\n                        if (err) return sendError(res, err);\n                        var b; try { b = parseJsonObject(text); } catch (e) { e.status = 400; return sendError(res, e); }\n                        var bq = { _shape: b._shape || q._shape, _nl: b._nl || q._nl };\n                        query(b.sql, b.params && typeof b.params === 'object' ? b.params : {}).then(function (d) { shaped(res, bq, d); }, function (e) { sendError(res, e); });\n                    });\n                }\n                if (q.sql != null) return query([].concat(q.sql)[0], paramsFrom(q)).then(function (d) { shaped(res, q, d); }, function (e) { sendError(res, e); });\n                return query(Q.SCHEMA_SQL, {}, MAX_ROWS).then(function (d) {\n                    send(res, 200, { ok: true, database: name, tables: Q.schemaOf(d.rows) });\n                }, function (e) { sendError(res, e); });\n            }\n            if ((m = new RegExp('^/' + name + '/(.+?)(\\\\.json)?$').exec(p))) {\n                var t = Q.tableQuery(m[1], q, cfg().maxRows);\n                return query(t.sql, t.params, t.size + 1).then(function (d) {\n                    var more = d.rows.length > t.size; if (more) d.rows = d.rows.slice(0, t.size);\n                    var next = more ? String(t.offset + t.size) : null, nq = {};\n                    if (next) { Object.keys(q).forEach(function (k) { if (k !== '_key') nq[k] = q[k]; }); nq._next = next; }\n                    d.truncated = false;\n                    shaped(res, q, d, { table: m[1], next: next, next_url: next ? p + '?' + querystring.stringify(nq) : null });\n                }, function (e) { sendError(res, e); });\n            }\n            send(res, 404, { ok: false, error: 'Not found. Try /' + name + '.json?sql=select+1', status: 404, title: 'Not found' });\n        } catch (e) {\n            try { sendError(res, e); } catch (x) { try { res.end(); } catch (y) { /* gone */ } }\n        }\n    }\n\n    function listen() {\n        var c = cfg();\n        listenError = null;\n        try {\n            var srv = server = http.createServer(handle);\n            srv.maxConnections = MAX_SOCKETS;\n            srv.timeout = MAX_TIMEOUT + 30000;\n            srv.on('connection', function (s) { sockets.push(s); s.on('close', function () { var i = sockets.indexOf(s); if (i >= 0) sockets.splice(i, 1); }); });\n            srv.on('error', function (e) { if (srv !== server) return; listenError = String(e && e.message || e); running = false; try { srv.close(); } catch (x) { /* not open */ } });\n            srv.on('listening', function () { if (srv === server) running = true; });\n            srv.listen(c.port, '0.0.0.0');\n        } catch (e) { listenError = String(e && e.message || e); server = null; }\n    }\n    function close() {\n        running = false;\n        if (server) { try { server.close(); } catch (e) { /* already closed */ } server = null; }\n        sockets.slice().forEach(function (s) { try { s.destroy(); } catch (e) { /* gone */ } });\n        sockets = [];\n    }\n\n    function state() {\n        var c = cfg();\n        return { running: running, port: c.port, addresses: lanAddresses(), database: dbName(c.dbPath), dbPath: c.dbPath, cors: c.cors,\n            timeoutMs: c.timeoutMs, maxRows: c.maxRows, apiKey: apiKey(), sqliteVersion: sqliteVersion, problem: listenError || probeError,\n            lastError: lastError, queries: counts.queries, denied: counts.denied, pending: queue.length + (busy ? 1 : 0) };\n    }\n    function json(res, body, code) { res.writeHead(code || 200, { 'content-type': 'application/json', 'cache-control': 'no-store' }); res.end(JSON.stringify(body)); }\n\n    return {\n        start: function () {\n            stopped = false; page = loadPage(ctx); apiKey(); listen();\n            probe().then(null, function () { /* recorded in probeError */ });\n        },\n        stop: function () {\n            stopped = true; close(); page = null;\n            var waiting = queue; queue = [];\n            waiting.forEach(function (w) { var e = new Error('The Shard was switched off'); e.status = 503; w.reject(e); });\n        },\n        status: function () { var c = cfg(); return { running: running, port: c.port, sqlite: sqliteVersion, queries: counts.queries, problem: listenError || probeError || undefined }; },\n\n        // The dashboard page and its settings. These routes are Vetro's (paired device or page token), not the API's.\n        route: function (req, res, sub) {\n            if (sub === 'ui' && req.method === 'GET') { res.writeHead(200, { 'content-type': 'text/html; charset=utf-8', 'cache-control': 'no-store' }); res.end(page || loadPage(ctx)); return true; }\n            if (sub === 'state' && req.method === 'GET') { json(res, state()); return true; }\n            if (req.method !== 'POST') return false;\n            if (sub === 'probe') { probe().then(function (s) { json(res, s); }, function (e) { json(res, { ok: false, error: String(e && e.message || e) }, 500); }); return true; }\n            if (sub === 'regen-key') { try { save({ apiKey: newKey() }); json(res, state()); } catch (e) { json(res, { ok: false, error: e.message }, 500); } return true; }\n            if (sub === 'settings' || sub === 'query') {\n                readBody(req, function (err, text) {\n                    var b;\n                    try { if (err) throw err; b = parseJsonObject(text); } catch (e) { return json(res, { ok: false, error: e.message }, 400); }\n                    if (sub === 'query') {\n                        return query(b.sql, b.params && typeof b.params === 'object' ? b.params : {}).then(function (d) {\n                            json(res, { ok: true, columns: d.columns, rows: d.rows, truncated: d.truncated, query_ms: d.ms });\n                        }, function (e) { json(res, { ok: false, error: String(e && e.message || e) }, e && e.status || 500); });\n                    }\n                    var patch = {}, bad = null, before = cfg();\n                    if (b.port != null) { if (typeof b.port === 'number' && b.port >= 1024 && b.port <= 65535 && b.port % 1 === 0) patch.port = b.port; else bad = 'Port must be 1024-65535'; }\n                    if (b.dbPath != null) { if (validPath(b.dbPath)) patch.dbPath = b.dbPath; else bad = 'Database path must be absolute, letters, digits, . _ - / only'; }\n                    if (b.cors != null) { if (validOrigin(b.cors)) patch.cors = b.cors; else bad = 'CORS origin must be *, empty, or like http://host:port'; }\n                    if (b.timeoutMs != null) { if (typeof b.timeoutMs === 'number' && b.timeoutMs >= 1000 && b.timeoutMs <= MAX_TIMEOUT) patch.timeoutMs = b.timeoutMs; else bad = 'Time limit must be 1-30 s'; }\n                    if (b.maxRows != null) { if (typeof b.maxRows === 'number' && b.maxRows >= 1 && b.maxRows <= MAX_ROWS) patch.maxRows = b.maxRows; else bad = 'Row limit must be 1-' + MAX_ROWS; }\n                    if (bad) return json(res, { ok: false, error: bad }, 400);\n                    try { save(patch); } catch (e) { return json(res, { ok: false, error: 'Settings could not be saved: ' + e.message }, 500); }\n                    if (!stopped && patch.port && patch.port !== before.port) { close(); listen(); }\n                    if (patch.dbPath && patch.dbPath !== before.dbPath) return probe().then(function (s) { json(res, s); });\n                    json(res, state());\n                });\n                return true;\n            }\n            return false;\n        }\n    };\n};\nmodule.exports.VERSION = VERSION;\n","sql.js":"'use strict';\n// The query side of the Art SQL API: checks a client's SQL, fills in its :named parameters, builds the sqlite3\n// command that runs it read-only as root (through ctx.execute), and parses the answer. No I/O here, so it can be\n// tested on its own. Plain ES5: older TVs run Node 4.4.\n//\n// Why the checks matter: the query runs in the TV's own sqlite3 *shell* (3.33.0 on the tested TV), as root. -readonly\n// stops writes to the database, but the shell adds functions and tables that reach the file system, and 3.33 has no\n// -safe flag (3.37+) to turn them off:\n//   readfile(), writefile(), edit(), fsdir(), zipfile    read, write or list any file as root\n//   load_extension()                                     loads native code as root\n//   ATTACH, VACUUM INTO, temp_store_directory            open or create other files\n//   sha3_query()                                         runs SQL built from a string, past these checks\n//   fts3_tokenizer()                                     known memory-safety hazard\n// So: one statement only; it must start with SELECT, WITH, VALUES, PRAGMA or EXPLAIN; SELECT/WITH/VALUES are wrapped as\n// a subquery (which also enforces \"one statement\" and lets us cap the rows); and any of the words below anywhere in\n// the text, quoted or not, rejects the query. A string literal is scanned too, because SQLite accepts a quoted name\n// as a table-valued function ('fsdir'('/')).\n\nvar BLOCKED = ['attach', 'detach', 'vacuum', 'readfile', 'writefile', 'edit', 'fsdir', 'zipfile', 'load_extension',\n    'sha3_query', 'fts3_tokenizer', 'temp_store_directory', 'data_store_directory'];\nvar BLOCKED_RE = new RegExp('(^|[^a-z0-9_$])(' + BLOCKED.join('|') + ')(?![a-z0-9_$])', 'i');\nvar WRAPPED = { select: 1, 'with': 1, values: 1 }, RAW = { pragma: 1, explain: 1 };\nvar MAX_SQL = 32768, MAX_PARAM = 65536;\n\nfunction bytes(s) { return Buffer.from && Buffer.from !== Uint8Array.from ? Buffer.from(s) : new Buffer(s); }\nfunction shQuote(s) { return \"'\" + String(s).replace(/'/g, \"'\\\\''\") + \"'\"; }\nfunction literal(v) { return \"'\" + String(v).replace(/'/g, \"''\") + \"'\"; }\nfunction ident(name) { return '\"' + String(name).replace(/\"/g, '\"\"') + '\"'; }\nfunction fail(message, title) { var e = new Error(message); e.title = title || 'Invalid SQL'; e.status = 400; return e; }\n\n// One pass over the SQL that knows about strings, quoted names and comments. It returns the first keyword, where\n// each top-level ';' is, and every :name parameter outside strings and comments (Datasette's syntax). Parentheses\n// must balance, so a query cannot close the SELECT * FROM ( ... ) it is wrapped in.\nfunction scan(sql) {\n    var i = 0, n = sql.length, first = null, semis = [], params = [], depth = 0, c, end, close;\n    while (i < n) {\n        c = sql.charAt(i);\n        if (c === '-' && sql.charAt(i + 1) === '-') { end = sql.indexOf('\\n', i); i = end < 0 ? n : end + 1; continue; }\n        if (c === '/' && sql.charAt(i + 1) === '*') { end = sql.indexOf('*/', i + 2); if (end < 0) throw fail('Unterminated /* comment'); i = end + 2; continue; }\n        if (c === \"'\" || c === '\"' || c === '`' || c === '[') {\n            close = c === '[' ? ']' : c; end = i + 1;\n            for (;;) {\n                end = sql.indexOf(close, end);\n                if (end < 0) throw fail('Unterminated ' + (c === \"'\" ? 'string' : 'quoted name'));\n                if (close !== ']' && sql.charAt(end + 1) === close) { end += 2; continue; }\n                break;\n            }\n            if (first === null) first = '';\n            i = end + 1; continue;\n        }\n        if (c === ';') { semis.push(i); i++; continue; }\n        if (c === '(') depth++;\n        if (c === ')' && --depth < 0) throw fail('Unbalanced parentheses');\n        if (c === ':' && /[A-Za-z_]/.test(sql.charAt(i + 1))) {\n            var m = /^:([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)/.exec(sql.slice(i));\n            params.push({ name: m[1], at: i, length: m[0].length }); i += m[0].length; continue;\n        }\n        if (/[A-Za-z_]/.test(c)) {\n            var w = /^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_$]*/.exec(sql.slice(i))[0];\n            if (first === null) first = w.toLowerCase();\n            i += w.length; continue;\n        }\n        if (first === null && !/\\s/.test(c)) first = '';\n        i++;\n    }\n    if (depth !== 0) throw fail('Unbalanced parentheses');\n    return { first: first || '', semis: semis, params: params };\n}\n\n// Only whitespace, comments and stray semicolons after position `from`? (Anything else there is a second statement.)\nfunction blankAfter(sql, from) { return !/[^\\s;]/.test(stripComments(sql.slice(from))); }\nfunction stripComments(s) { return s.replace(/--[^\\n]*(\\n|$)/g, ' ').replace(/\\/\\*[\\s\\S]*?\\*\\//g, ' '); }\n\n// Check a query and turn it into the SQL that is actually run. params: { name: value } (values become string\n// literals, like Datasette). maxRows: the cap; the SQL asks for one more so we can tell the result was truncated.\nfunction prepare(sql, params, maxRows) {\n    if (typeof sql !== 'string' || !sql.trim()) throw fail('Missing sql', 'Missing SQL');\n    if (sql.length > MAX_SQL) throw fail('SQL is longer than ' + MAX_SQL + ' characters');\n    if (/\\0/.test(sql)) throw fail('SQL contains a NUL character');\n    var hit = BLOCKED_RE.exec(sql);\n    if (hit) throw fail('\"' + hit[2] + '\" is not allowed: this API is read-only and cannot reach other files', 'Forbidden SQL');\n    var s = scan(sql);\n    if (!WRAPPED[s.first] && !RAW[s.first]) throw fail('Only SELECT, WITH, VALUES, PRAGMA and EXPLAIN statements are allowed', 'Forbidden SQL');\n    if (s.semis.length && !blankAfter(sql, s.semis[0] + 1)) throw fail('Only one statement per query');\n    var body = s.semis.length ? sql.slice(0, s.semis[0]) : sql;\n    if (s.first === 'pragma' && /=/.test(stripComments(body))) throw fail('PRAGMA can only read here (no \"=\")', 'Forbidden SQL');\n\n    params = params || {};\n    var out = '', last = 0, used = {};\n    for (var k = 0; k < s.params.length; k++) {\n        var p = s.params[k];\n        if (p.at >= body.length) break;\n        if (!Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(params, p.name) || params[p.name] == null) throw fail('Missing parameter :' + p.name, 'Missing parameter');\n        var v = String(params[p.name]);\n        if (v.length > MAX_PARAM || /\\0/.test(v)) throw fail('Parameter :' + p.name + ' is too long or contains a NUL character');\n        out += body.slice(last, p.at) + literal(v); last = p.at + p.length; used[p.name] = v;\n    }\n    out += body.slice(last);\n    var run = WRAPPED[s.first] ? 'SELECT * FROM (\\n' + out + '\\n) LIMIT ' + (maxRows + 1) : out;\n    return { sql: run, params: used, wrapped: !!WRAPPED[s.first], first: s.first };\n}\n\n// The shell command. The SQL travels base64-encoded so no character of it is ever seen by the shell; stdin is\n// /dev/null; .timeout waits up to 3 s when the Art app holds a write lock; .limit caps any one string or blob at\n// 10 MB so a query cannot make sqlite3 (running as root) eat the TV's memory.\nfunction command(sqlite, dbPath, sql) {\n    var b64 = bytes(sql).toString('base64');\n    return '__q=\"$(printf %s ' + b64 + ' | base64 -d)\"; exec ' + shQuote(sqlite) +\n        ' -readonly -batch -bail -cmd ' + shQuote('.timeout 3000') + ' -cmd ' + shQuote('.limit length 10000000') +\n        ' -cmd ' + shQuote('.mode json') + ' ' + shQuote(dbPath) + ' \"$__q\" </dev/null';\n}\n\n// sqlite3 -json prints one array per statement, nothing at all for no rows. EXPLAIN QUERY PLAN is the exception: the\n// shell always draws it as a text tree, so that comes back as one row per line, { plan: \"...\" }.\n// sqlite3 3.33 also echoes the .limit it was given (\"              length 10000000\") to stdout, before the results.\nfunction parseOutput(stdout, first) {\n    var text = String(stdout || '').replace(/^[ \\t]*length[ \\t]+\\d+[ \\t]*\\r?\\n?/, '').replace(/^\\s+|\\s+$/g, '');\n    if (!text) return [];\n    if (first === 'explain' && text.charAt(0) !== '[') return text.split('\\n').map(function (l) { return { plan: l }; });\n    try { var v = JSON.parse(text); return Array.isArray(v) ? v : []; } catch (e) { /* several statements: take the last */ }\n    var parts = JSON.parse('[' + text.replace(/\\]\\s*\\n\\s*\\[/g, '],[') + ']');\n    return parts.length ? parts[parts.length - 1] : [];\n}\nfunction columnsOf(rows) { return rows.length ? Object.keys(rows[0]) : []; }\n\n// sqlite3 writes \"Error: no such table: x\" (3.33) or \"Parse error in 11th command line argument: ...\" (newer): keep the useful part.\nfunction cleanError(stderr) {\n    var s = String(stderr || '').replace(/^\\s+|\\s+$/g, '').split('\\n')[0] || 'sqlite3 failed';\n    return s.replace(/^(Error|Parse error|Runtime error)( in \\S+ command line argument| near line \\d+)?:\\s*/, '').slice(0, 500);\n}\n\n// SQL for GET /<db>/<table>.json. Filters follow Datasette: ?col=value, ?col__gt=5, ?col__contains=x ...\nvar OPS = { exact: '= ?', not: '!= ?', gt: '> ?', gte: '>= ?', lt: '< ?', lte: '<= ?', like: 'LIKE ?', glob: 'GLOB ?',\n    contains: \"LIKE '%' || ? || '%'\", startswith: \"LIKE ? || '%'\", endswith: \"LIKE '%' || ?\" };\nfunction tableQuery(table, query, maxRows) {\n    var where = [], params = {}, n = 0;\n    Object.keys(query).forEach(function (key) {\n        if (key.charAt(0) === '_') return;\n        var vals = [].concat(query[key]), col = key, op = 'exact', m = /^(.+)__([a-z]+)$/.exec(key);\n        if (m && (OPS[m[2]] || m[2] === 'isnull' || m[2] === 'notnull')) { col = m[1]; op = m[2]; }\n        vals.forEach(function (v) {\n            if (op === 'isnull' || op === 'notnull') { where.push(ident(col) + (op === 'isnull' ? ' IS NULL' : ' IS NOT NULL')); return; }\n            var name = 'p' + (n++); params[name] = v;\n            where.push(ident(col) + ' ' + OPS[op].replace('?', ':' + name));\n        });\n    });\n    var size = parseInt(query._size, 10); if (!(size > 0)) size = Math.min(100, maxRows); size = Math.min(size, maxRows);\n    var offset = parseInt(query._next, 10); if (!(offset > 0)) offset = 0;\n    var sort = query._sort_desc || query._sort, order = sort ? ' ORDER BY ' + ident(sort) + (query._sort_desc ? ' DESC' : '') : '';\n    var sql = 'SELECT * FROM ' + ident(table) + (where.length ? ' WHERE ' + where.join(' AND ') : '') + order +\n        ' LIMIT ' + (size + 1) + ' OFFSET ' + offset;\n    return { sql: sql, params: params, size: size, offset: offset };\n}\n\nvar SCHEMA_SQL = \"SELECT m.name AS tbl, m.type AS type, p.name AS col FROM sqlite_master m JOIN pragma_table_info(m.name) p \" +\n    \"WHERE m.type IN ('table','view') AND m.name NOT LIKE 'sqlite_%' ORDER BY m.name, p.cid\";\nfunction schemaOf(rows) {\n    var out = [], byName = {};\n    rows.forEach(function (r) {\n        var t = byName[r.tbl];\n        if (!t) { t = byName[r.tbl] = { name: r.tbl, type: r.type, columns: [] }; out.push(t); }\n        t.columns.push(r.col);\n    });\n    return out;\n}\n\nmodule.exports = { prepare: prepare, scan: scan, command: command, parseOutput: parseOutput, columnsOf: columnsOf,\n    cleanError: cleanError, tableQuery: tableQuery, SCHEMA_SQL: SCHEMA_SQL, schemaOf: schemaOf, BLOCKED: BLOCKED, shQuote: shQuote };\n","ui.html":"<!doctype html>\n<html>\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"color-scheme\" content=\"light dark\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Art SQL API</title>\n<style>\n  :root { --fg: #1d1d1f; --muted: #6e6e73; --bg: #fff; --card: #f5f5f7; --line: #d2d2d7; --accent: #0a66c2; --bad: #c62828; --good: #2e7d32; }\n  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { :root { --fg: #f5f5f7; --muted: #a1a1a6; --bg: #1c1c1e; --card: #2c2c2e; --line: #3a3a3c; --accent: #64a8f0; --bad: #ef7070; --good: #7bc47f; } }\n  body { font: 15px/1.45 system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; color: var(--fg); background: var(--bg); margin: 20px; max-width: 980px; }\n  h2 { margin: 0 0 4px; } h3 { margin: 22px 0 8px; font-size: 15px; }\n  .muted { color: var(--muted); } .bad { color: var(--bad); } .good { color: var(--good); }\n  .card { background: var(--card); border-radius: 10px; padding: 12px 14px; margin: 10px 0; }\n  code, textarea, input, pre { font: 13px ui-monospace, Menlo, Consolas, monospace; }\n  code { background: var(--card); padding: 1px 4px; border-radius: 4px; }\n  textarea { width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; min-height: 90px; padding: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; background: var(--bg); color: var(--fg); }\n  input { padding: 5px 7px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px; background: var(--bg); color: var(--fg); }\n  button { font: inherit; padding: 6px 12px; border-radius: 7px; border: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--bg); color: var(--fg); cursor: pointer; }\n  button.primary { background: var(--accent); border-color: var(--accent); color: #fff; }\n  .row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px; align-items: center; margin: 6px 0; }\n  .grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr; gap: 6px 12px; align-items: center; }\n  .scroll { overflow: auto; max-height: 420px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; }\n  table { border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 13px; }\n  th, td { text-align: left; padding: 4px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); vertical-align: top; white-space: nowrap; max-width: 360px; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; }\n  th { position: sticky; top: 0; background: var(--card); }\n  pre { white-space: pre-wrap; word-break: break-all; margin: 6px 0; }\n  .tables span { display: inline-block; margin: 2px 6px 2px 0; }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<h2>Art SQL API</h2>\n<div class=\"muted\">Read-only SQL over the Art app's database, for other apps on your network. JSON follows a subset of Datasette's API.</div>\n\n<div class=\"card\" id=\"status\">Loading…</div>\n\n<h3>Connect</h3>\n<div class=\"card\">\n  <div class=\"grid\">\n    <span class=\"muted\">Endpoint</span><code id=\"endpoint\">…</code>\n    <span class=\"muted\">API key</span>\n    <span class=\"row\" style=\"margin:0\"><code id=\"key\">••••••••</code><button id=\"show\">Show</button><button id=\"regen\">New key</button></span>\n  </div>\n  <pre id=\"example\" class=\"muted\"></pre>\n</div>\n\n<h3>Try a query</h3>\n<textarea id=\"sql\" spellcheck=\"false\">select name from sqlite_master where type = 'table' order by name</textarea>\n<div class=\"row\"><button class=\"primary\" id=\"run\">Run</button><span id=\"qinfo\" class=\"muted\"></span></div>\n<div id=\"result\"></div>\n<div id=\"tables\" class=\"tables muted\"></div>\n\n<h3>Settings</h3>\n<div class=\"card grid\">\n  <span class=\"muted\">Port</span><input id=\"port\" type=\"number\" min=\"1024\" max=\"65535\" style=\"width:90px\">\n  <span class=\"muted\">Database</span><input id=\"dbPath\" style=\"width:100%\">\n  <span class=\"muted\">CORS origin</span><input id=\"cors\" placeholder=\"* or http://host:port, empty for none\" style=\"width:280px\">\n  <span class=\"muted\">Time limit (s)</span><input id=\"timeout\" type=\"number\" min=\"1\" max=\"30\" style=\"width:70px\">\n  <span class=\"muted\">Row limit</span><input id=\"maxRows\" type=\"number\" min=\"1\" max=\"5000\" style=\"width:90px\">\n  <span></span><span class=\"row\" style=\"margin:0\"><button id=\"saveSettings\">Save</button><button id=\"probe\">Check sqlite3</button><span id=\"sinfo\" class=\"muted\"></span></span>\n</div>\n\n<script>\nvar S = null, keyShown = false;\nfunction $(id) { return document.getElementById(id); }\nfunction esc(s) { return String(s).replace(/[&<>\"]/g, function (c) { return { '&': '&amp;', '<': '&lt;', '>': '&gt;', '\"': '&quot;' }[c]; }); }\nfunction post(sub, body) {\n  return fetch(sub, { method: 'POST', headers: { 'Content-Type': 'text/plain' }, body: JSON.stringify(body || {}) })\n    .then(function (r) { return r.json(); });\n}\nfunction base() { var a = (S.addresses && S.addresses[0]) || 'TV-IP'; return 'http://' + a + ':' + S.port; }\nfunction render(s) {\n  if (!s || s.ok === false) { $('sinfo').textContent = (s && s.error) || 'Error'; return; }\n  S = s;\n  var bits = [];\n  bits.push(s.running ? '<b class=\"good\">Listening</b> on port ' + s.port : '<b class=\"bad\">Not listening</b>');\n  bits.push(s.sqliteVersion ? 'sqlite3 ' + esc(s.sqliteVersion) : 'sqlite3 not checked yet');\n  bits.push(s.queries + (s.queries === 1 ? ' query' : ' queries') + (s.denied ? ', ' + s.denied + ' refused (wrong key)' : ''));\n  var html = bits.join(' · ');\n  if (s.problem) html += '<div class=\"bad\">' + esc(s.problem) + '</div>';\n  else if (s.lastError) html += '<div class=\"muted\">Last error: ' + esc(s.lastError) + '</div>';\n  $('status').innerHTML = html;\n  $('endpoint').textContent = base() + '/' + s.database + '.json';\n  $('key').textContent = keyShown ? s.apiKey : '••••••••';\n  $('example').textContent =\n    'curl -H \"Authorization: Bearer ' + (keyShown ? s.apiKey : '<key>') + '\" \\\\\\n  \"' + base() + '/' + s.database + '.json?sql=select+name+from+sqlite_master&_shape=array\"\\n\\n' +\n    'Tables: ' + base() + '/' + s.database + '.json\\nOne table: ' + base() + '/' + s.database + '/<table>.json?_size=50';\n  if (document.activeElement && document.activeElement.tagName === 'INPUT') return;\n  $('port').value = s.port; $('dbPath').value = s.dbPath; $('cors').value = s.cors;\n  $('timeout').value = Math.round(s.timeoutMs / 1000); $('maxRows').value = s.maxRows;\n}\nfunction refresh() { return fetch('state').then(function (r) { return r.json(); }).then(render, function (e) { $('status').textContent = 'Could not reach the Shard: ' + e; }); }\n\nfunction table(d) {\n  if (!d.rows.length) return '<div class=\"muted\">No rows.</div>';\n  var cols = d.columns, h = '<div class=\"scroll\"><table><tr>' + cols.map(function (c) { return '<th>' + esc(c) + '</th>'; }).join('') + '</tr>';\n  d.rows.forEach(function (r) {\n    h += '<tr>' + cols.map(function (c) { var v = r[c]; return '<td title=\"' + esc(v == null ? 'NULL' : v) + '\">' + (v == null ? '<span class=\"muted\">NULL</span>' : esc(v)) + '</td>'; }).join('') + '</tr>';\n  });\n  return h + '</table></div>';\n}\nfunction run() {\n  $('qinfo').textContent = 'Running…'; $('result').innerHTML = '';\n  post('query', { sql: $('sql').value }).then(function (d) {\n    if (!d.ok) { $('qinfo').textContent = ''; $('result').innerHTML = '<div class=\"bad\">' + esc(d.error) + '</div>'; return; }\n    $('qinfo').textContent = d.rows.length + ' row' + (d.rows.length === 1 ? '' : 's') + (d.truncated ? ' (truncated at the row limit)' : '') + ' · ' + d.query_ms + ' ms';\n    $('result').innerHTML = table(d);\n    refresh();\n  }, function (e) { $('qinfo').textContent = ''; $('result').innerHTML = '<div class=\"bad\">' + esc(e) + '</div>'; });\n}\nfunction loadTables() {\n  post('query', { sql: \"select name from sqlite_master where type in ('table','view') and name not like 'sqlite_%' order by name\" }).then(function (d) {\n    if (!d.ok || !d.rows.length) return;\n    $('tables').innerHTML = 'Tables: ' + d.rows.map(function (r) { return '<span><a href=\"#\" data-t=\"' + esc(r.name) + '\">' + esc(r.name) + '</a></span>'; }).join('');\n  });\n}\n$('tables').onclick = function (e) {\n  var t = e.target.getAttribute && e.target.getAttribute('data-t'); if (!t) return;\n  e.preventDefault(); $('sql').value = 'select * from \"' + t.replace(/\"/g, '\"\"') + '\" limit 50'; run();\n};\n$('run').onclick = run;\n$('sql').onkeydown = function (e) { if ((e.metaKey || e.ctrlKey) && e.key === 'Enter') run(); };\n$('show').onclick = function () { keyShown = !keyShown; $('show').textContent = keyShown ? 'Hide' : 'Show'; render(S); };\n$('regen').onclick = function () {\n  if (!confirm('Make a new API key? Apps using the old one stop working until you give them the new key.')) return;\n  post('regen-key').then(function (s) { keyShown = true; $('show').textContent = 'Hide'; render(s); });\n};\n$('saveSettings').onclick = function () {\n  $('sinfo').textContent = 'Saving…';\n  post('settings', { port: +$('port').value, dbPath: $('dbPath').value, cors: $('cors').value, timeoutMs: +$('timeout').value * 1000, maxRows: +$('maxRows').value })\n    .then(function (s) { if (s.ok === false) { $('sinfo').textContent = s.error; return; } $('sinfo').textContent = 'Saved'; document.activeElement.blur(); render(s); setTimeout(refresh, 600); });\n};\n$('probe').onclick = function () { $('sinfo').textContent = 'Checking…'; post('probe').then(function (s) { $('sinfo').textContent = ''; render(s); }); };\nrefresh().then(function () { loadTables(); });\nsetInterval(refresh, 10000);\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n"}}
